Lately I've been playing tourists.  My early game skills are weak so
I'm
trying characters that start out weak to teach myself to improve those
skills.  Sometimes a lesson should have been learned long ago.

My tourist was descending very slowly trying to keep his current XP
level 2 larger than his current depth.  It meant a lot of wandering
around eating corpses and occasionally praying to handle hunger.
I failed to track the turn of the last prayer and was Hungry so I was
eating any non-poisonous corpse.  So without thinking I ate a nymph
corpse.  "You feel jumpy".  Ooops.

In spite of teleportitis I continued exploring down into the mines.  I
picked up any corpse I intended to eat.  Got poison resistance, even
managed to eat a fresh tengu without getting TC.

The problem with teleportitis is it limits your ability to retreat to a
corridor to face hordes or nasties.  Especially problematic in the
mines.
My first encounter with an ettin mummy (likely polymorph trap on the
level) caused my hit points to plummet so I fled.  Throwing darts or
daggers made the mummy catch up so I just ran.  And then I teleported
one square away.  "The ettin mummy hits! DYWYPI?"

Primary lesson - When eating corpses it is NOT good enough to just
avoid poisonous ones until getting poson resistance.

Secondary lesson - When encountering a monster well out of depth
run and gauge the ratio of your moves to its moves *before* starting
to throw missiles.  A sufficiently nasty monster will take out too
many hit points with one hit to allow even a single melee hit.

Tertiary lesson - Maybe enhancing dart once isn't a bad idea for a
tourist.  They do have skill slots to spare.  Enhancing dagger to
Expert as soon as daggers came available worked but I still had
too few daggers at that point to take out an ettin mummy before
running out.



